# UI/UX DESIGN SYSTEM RULES (STRICT ENFORCEMENT)

## 1. COLOR PALETTE ENFORCEMENT
- **FORBIDDEN COLORS:** You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from using `#000000` (Pure Black), `bg-black`, `text-black`, `border-black`, or generic `gray-900` / `zinc-900` for dark backgrounds.
- **PRIMARY BACKGROUND:** The "Dark Mode" background is NOT black. It is the established **Brand Dark Blue** (use CSS variables: `--color-bg-primary`, `--background`, or Tailwind `surface.primary` / `clinical-navy` / Slate-950 `#020617` / `#0f172a`).
- **TEXT ON DARK:** Never use pure white (`#FFFFFF`) on the Dark Blue background for large areas (causes eye strain). Use `slate-50` or `slate-100` (off-white) or `var(--color-text-primary)`.
- **TEXT ON DARK (SECONDARY):** Never use generic gray for secondary text on dark backgrounds. Use **Blue-tinted Grays** (e.g., Tailwind `text-slate-400` or `text-blue-200/50` or `var(--color-text-muted)`) to prevent "muddy" contrast.

## 2. SHADOWS & DEPTH
- **NO BLACK SHADOWS:** Do not use default `shadow-lg` if it utilizes black. Prefer semantic variables.
- **COLORED SHADOWS:** Generate shadows using the primary brand blue with high transparency (e.g., `shadow-[0_10px_40px_-10px_rgba(15,23,42,0.5)]` or `var(--color-shadow-brand)`).
- **GLASSMORPHISM:** When creating overlays, use `backdrop-blur-md` combined with `bg-[var(--color-bg-primary)]/80` or `bg-[var(--color-bg-secondary)]/90` rather than solid black.

## 3. CHART & DATA VISUALIZATION
- **PALETTE:** All charts (Recharts/Chart.js) must use a monochromatic or analogous color scale derived from the Brand Blue (use `lib/chartTheme.tsx` colors/gradients).
- **GRID LINES:** Grid lines on charts must be faint blue-gray (e.g., `stroke-slate-700/20` or `var(--chart-grid-stroke)`), NEVER pure gray or black. Prefer horizontal grid only or 10% opacity for vertical lines.

## 4. COMPONENT CONSTRUCTION
- **BORDERS:** Dark mode borders must be `border-slate-700` or `border-slate-800` (Dark Blue-Gray), never `border-gray-800`. Use `var(--color-border)` for theme safety.
- **SKELETON LOADERS:** Skeleton pulse animations must use `bg-slate-800` to `bg-slate-700` (Blue-Gray), not generic gray.
- **FOCUS RINGS:** Override `:focus-visible` with a glowing Cyan or Gold (complementary to Brand Blue), not default browser blue/black.

## 5. BUTTON HIERARCHY
- **One Primary Action per Screen:** Only the main call-to-action for the current view should be solid primary (e.g., "Start Session"). Header actions like "Build Session" or "Backup data" should be secondary (outlined or ghost) when they are not the primary goal of the page.

## 6. LAYOUT & ALIGNMENT
- **GLOBAL GRID:** Use a consistent max-width container (e.g., `max-w-[1200px] mx-auto`) so that section headers, tabs, and card content align to the same vertical guideline.
